\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. There is a fountain filled with blood
\par Dawn from Immanuel's veins;
\par And sinners plunged beneath that flood,
\par Lose all their guilty stains.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The dying thief rejoiced to see
\par That fountain in His day;
\par And there may I, though vile as he,
\par Wash all my sins away.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O dying Lamp, Thy precious blood 
\par Shall never lose its power,
\par Still all ransomed church of God
\par Be saved to sin no more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. E'er since, by faith, I saw the stream
\par Thy flowing wounds supply,
\par Redeeming love has been my theme
\par And shall be till I die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then in a nobler, sweeter song
\par I'll sing Thy power to save,
\par When this poor lisping, stammering tongue
\par Lies silent in the grave.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

